# Jaecoo 8 five-door large SUV, 2026 onwards.
#
# The Jaecoo 8: the largest of the three, with the tall vertical-slat grille,
# the slim lamps and the full-width tail bar. It was announced on 11 March
# 2026 and went on sale in May 2026. The 'Jaecoo 9' name used in some markets
# is recorded as an ambiguity.
# https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jaecoo_8
#
# Dimensions 4.820 x 1.930 x 1.699 m, wheelbase 2.820 m.
#
# Shape reference: image 1 is a manufacturer studio side view, perpendicular
# and level; the front and rear views are UK-registered press cars. All four
# are manufacturer press images; no independent UK photograph exists yet.
#
# Colours: grade (a), the JAECOO UK palette: Granite White, Basalt Black,
# Iced Slate Grey and Anthracite Silver. Weights 12, 10, 10, 8, total 40,
# provisional.
#
# Speed 200 km/h. Comfort 95/322, on the line 180 + 1.5 x 95. Classes 3,4.
# Dates are road presence: 2026 intro, retires staggered 2046-2049.
#
# Metres master: citycars/4.5/jaecoo-8.blend. Interchange:
# citycars/4.5/jaecoo-8.dae. References:
# citycars/references/jaecoo-8/ (gitignored; manufacturer press images held
# as internal reference only).
#
# Accepted deviations: the wheel spokes, lamp internals, badges and door
# surfacing are simplified. The published 2.820 m wheelbase takes precedence
# over the wheelbase-to-length ratio measured in the side image.


obj=citycar
name=Jaecoo8(GraniteWhite)
copyright=JamesPetts

DistributionWeight=12
intro_year=2026
intro_month=5
retire_year=2049
retire_month=6
speed=200
class=3,4
maximum_comfortable_journey_minutes=95
maximum_tolerable_journey_minutes=322

